      "score": 1,
      "reason": "The first 3s are a calm greeting and a contextual question (\"Who is this?\") from a housekeeper. There is no action, shock, or cruel line to stop a scroller."
    },
    "cliffhanger": {
      "score": 1,
      "reason": "It ends after the conflict has passed: the Housekeeper leaves, Prudence says \"That was close,\" and Juliana asks \"Where is the West Wing?\" This is resolved and transitional, not an unresolved peak."
    },
    "questions": [
      {"q": "Why is Lady Juliana disguised as a maid?", "type": "confusion"},
      {"q": "What is in the West Wing?", "type": "intrigue"}
